 enhanced financial flexibility without altering ABFRL's shareholding.","summary":"Aditya Birla Fashion and Retail (ABFRL) approved the merger of two wholly-owned subsidiaries, Jaypore and TG Apparel & Decor.\nThe merger aims for operational simplification, cost reduction, and enhanced financial flexibility without altering ABFRL's shareholding.","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7f0906-2517-42c3-abf5-90d8fc86e917.pdf","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-02-05T19:01:01","source":"BSE"},{"id":"474113","title":"ABFRL reported Q3 net loss of ₹152.2 crore, wider than ₹51.3 crore YoY; revenue grew 7.9% to ₹2,373.6 crore.\nEBITDA rose 2.4% to ₹308.6 crore; EBITDA margin declined to 13% from 13.7%. Shares ended 3% higher but fell 6% YTD.","summary":"ABFRL reported Q3 net loss of ₹152.2 crore, wider than ₹51.3 crore YoY; revenue grew 7.9% to ₹2,373.6 crore.\nEBITDA rose 2.4% to ₹308.6 crore; EBITDA margin declined to 13% from 13.7%. Shares ended 3% higher but fell 6% YTD.","url":"https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/earnings/abfrls-sales-grow-but-losses-deepen-in-q3-even-as-stock-ends-higher-ws-l-19843428.htm","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-02-05T18:53:28","source":"CNBC TV 18"},{"id":"473928","title":"Aditya Birla Fashion's Q3 net loss widened to ₹1.5B from ₹513M YoY.\nRevenue increased to ₹24B from ₹22B YoY, showing growth despite losses.","summary":"Aditya Birla Fashion's Q3 net loss widened to ₹1.5B from ₹513M YoY.\nRevenue increased to ₹24B from ₹22B YoY, showing growth despite losses.","url":"","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-02-05T18:26:22","source":"Livesquawk"},{"id":"458244","title":"Aditya Birla Fashion announces CEO change; Anant Kumar Daga resigns from TCNS Division effective April 30, 2026.\nSooraj Bhat, current CEO of Ethnic Business, will take over TCNS responsibilities from May 1, 2026.","summary":"Aditya Birla Fashion announces CEO change; Anant Kumar Daga resigns from TCNS Division effective April 30, 2026.\nSooraj Bhat, current CEO of Ethnic Business, will take over TCNS responsibilities from May 1, 2026.","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=ecfed2f4-5123-4804-9874-0830751e79f4.pdf","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-01-29T13:07:37","source":"BSE"},{"id":"804333678320163072","title":"ABFRL's subsidiary invested INR 42.38 Cr in Wrogn Pvt Ltd, acquiring 2.53% stake for INR 6.57 Cr.\nA primary capital infusion of INR 35.8 Cr was made; Wrogn's FY25 revenue was INR 223.2 Cr.","summary":"ABFRL's subsidiary invested INR 42.38 Cr in Wrogn Pvt Ltd, acquiring 2.53% stake for INR 6.57 Cr.\nA primary capital infusion of INR 35.8 Cr was made; Wrogn's FY25 revenue was INR 223.2 Cr.","url":"https://sqst.in/veAf7","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-01-28T18:24:52","source":"ScoutQuest"},{"id":"457169","title":"Aditya Birla Digital Fashion Ventures Ltd invested in Wrogn, acquiring 2.53% for INR 6.57 Cr and INR 35.81 Cr via OCRPS.\nWrogn, a fashion brand, reported FY25 revenue of INR 223.23 Cr. The acquisition expands ABDFVL's digital-first brand portfolio.","summary":"Aditya Birla Digital Fashion Ventures Ltd invested in Wrogn, acquiring 2.53% for INR 6.57 Cr and INR 35.81 Cr via OCRPS.\nWrogn, a fashion brand, reported FY25 revenue of INR 223.23 Cr. The acquisition expands ABDFVL's digital-first brand portfolio.","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=f16026c8-1dea-4cdf-99b2-eedddd88429b.pdf","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-01-28T18:23:18","source":"BSE"},{"id":"801748272026974848","title":"Aditya Birla Fashion faces Rs 217 lakh demand from customs over IGST dispute.\nThe company plans to legally contest the demand order at CESTAT.","summary":"Aditya Birla Fashion faces Rs 217 lakh demand from customs over IGST dispute.\nThe company plans to legally contest the demand order at CESTAT.","url":"https://sqst.in/Z0jBk","imageUrl":null,"pubDate":"2026-01-21T15:11:23","source":"ScoutQuest"},{"id":"801298019446657664","title":"Aditya Birla Fashion shares fell 8% after